wifi: brcmfmac: accept bss_info versions above 112

Apple's Wi-Fi firmware from macOS Tahoe (26.x) reports a bss_info struct
version of 116. brcmfmac rejects anything outside 109..112, so every scan
fails with

  brcmf_inform_bss: BSS info version 116 unsupported

and the interface returns no results at all -- Wi-Fi is completely dead. This
affects any machine whose vendor firmware has been extracted from a recent
macOS, and it is silent: scans simply come back empty.

The struct is append-only. Hector Martin, on the thread that added v112
support, notes that "the offsets of the subsequent fields ... haven't
changed", and that older versions were retrofitted as compatible with newer
ones on exactly that basis:

  https://lkml.iu.edu/hypermail/linux/kernel/2311.0/05603.html

The fields brcmfmac reads therefore sit at fixed offsets and newer revisions
only append, so raising the ceiling is safe rather than speculative.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fwil_types.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/fwil_types.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 #define BRCMF_ARP_OL_PEER_AUTO_REPLY	0x00000008

 #define	BRCMF_BSS_INFO_MIN_VERSION	109 /* min ver of brcmf_bss_info_le struct */
-#define	BRCMF_BSS_INFO_MAX_VERSION	112 /* max ver of brcmf_bss_info_le struct */
+#define	BRCMF_BSS_INFO_MAX_VERSION	116 /* max ver of brcmf_bss_info_le struct */
 #define BRCMF_BSS_RSSI_ON_CHANNEL	0x0004

 #define BRCMF_STA_BRCM			0x00000001	/* Running a Broadcom driver */
